Based on the provided context, the factors (criteria) the Commission shall take into account to determine that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to high impact capabilities include:
(a) the number of parameters of the model;
(b) the quality or size of the data set, for example measured through tokens;
(c) the type of inputs and outputs (e.g. biological sequences);
(d) the benchmarks and evaluations of capabilities of the model, including considering the number of tasks without additional training, adaptability to learn new, distinct tasks, its level of autonomy and scalability, and the tools it has access to;
(e) whether it has a high impact on the internal market due to its reach (which is presumed when made available to at least 10,000 registered business users established in the Union);
(f) the number of registered end-users.

Additionally, the Commission may designate a model as presenting systemic risks ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel on the basis of criteria set out in Annex XIII.

Regarding whether the provider can challenge it:
1. When notifying the Commission that a model meets the condition, the provider may present "sufficiently substantiated arguments to demonstrate that, exceptionally, although it meets that requirement, the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks and therefore should not be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk."
2. Upon a reasoned request from a provider whose model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk, the Commission shall take the request into account and may decide to reassess whether the model can still be considered to present systemic risks. Such a request must contain objective, detailed, and new reasons that have arisen since the designation decision, and can be requested at the earliest six months after the designation decision (or six months after a previous reassessment decision where the designation was maintained).
